  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Rate of convergence in the central limit theorem for the determinantal point process with Bessel kernel — We consider a family of linear operators diagonalized by the Hankel transform.\n\n**Rate of convergence in the central limit theorem for the determinantal point process with Bessel kernel**\n\n*Matematicheski˘ı Sbornik*\n\n26 pp, 10 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We consider a family of linear operators diagonalized by the Hankel transform. We express explicitly the Fredholm determinants of these operators, as restricted to L2[0, R], so that the rate of their conver- gence as R →∞can be found. We use the link between these determinants and the distribution of additive functionals in a determinantal point process with Bessel kernel and estimate the distance in the Kolmogorov–Smirnov metric between the distribution of these functionals and the Gaussian dis- tribution. Bibliography: 27 titles.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; §1 Introduction; §2 Statement of the result; §3 Structure of the paper; §4 Trace class and Hilbert–Schmidt operators; §5 A link between the Bessel operator and the ; §6 Wiener–Hopf factorization on $H_1(\\mathbb{R; §7 Proof of Lemma 3; §8 Proof of Theorems 1 and 2; Bibliography",
      "lang": "en",
